- Demolishing old components;
- Reinstalling and adjusting existing detention doors;
- Applying security caulking;
- Anchoring hardware installation; and
- Performing full operational testing.

All work must maintain facility security at all times, with doors being removed one at a time as they are actively worked on.
Period of Performance: The contract is expected to begin on October 1, 2026, and continue through September 30, 2027. The County has the option to renew this Agreement for three additional one-year periods.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the Alachua County Jail located at 3333 NE 39th Ave, Gainesville, FL 32609.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be qualified and capable of performing the required services while adhering to all applicable laws and industry best practices. They must provide a bid bond equal to at least five percent (5%) of the bid amount. Bidders are required to demonstrate good faith efforts to utilize certified Small Business Enterprises (SBEs) for at least 15% of the dollar value of the bid. Additionally, bidders must comply with Alachua County Government Minimum Wage regulations.

