Background: The City of Pompano Beach is seeking bids for Well Rehabilitation and Maintenance to secure firm, fixed pricing and establish a term contract for well maintenance services for its Water Utilities. This initiative aims to ensure the reliability and efficiency of the city's water supply system.
Work Details: The contract involves providing well rehabilitation and maintenance services, which may include but are not limited to: 
- Inspection, cleaning, repair, and rehabilitation of existing wells; 
- Installation of new well components; 
- Ensuring compliance with local regulations; 
- Providing necessary documentation and reporting on the work performed. 

Bidders must demonstrate experience in municipal public supply well projects completed within the last five years.
Period of Performance: The initial term of the contract will commence upon approval by the City Commission and will last for three years. There is an option to renew for up to two additional one-year periods, contingent upon written notice from the contractor at least 90 days before the expiration of the current term.
Place of Performance: Services will be performed within the geographic limits of Pompano Beach, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be registered on the City’s eBid System. They must provide proof of being a licensed Water Well Contractor in Florida and a Licensed Florida State General Contractor. Bidders must submit a Bid Security Bond of at least 5% of the bid amount, evidence of prior project experience with municipal wells, and references from previous clients. Additional requirements include maintaining a satisfactory performance record, financial solvency, and compliance with all applicable laws.

Background: The City of Plant City is initiating a utility relocation project in preparation for the planned demolition of an old public works building that currently houses the electrical and fiber terminations for a nearby communication tower. 

The goal of this contract is to maintain continuous operations by provisioning a dedicated power supply and re-routing fiber optic connectivity to bypass the building, ensuring uninterrupted service and preserving network integrity.
Work Details: The scope of work includes: 
A. Relocating the existing generator; 
B. Installing a new electrical service and standby generator for the communications tower; 
C. Installing a new radio cabinet to house existing radios currently mounted on one of the tower legs; 
D. Installing new OT and IT fiber optic cabling routed through existing and newly constructed duct banks; 
E. Constructing new telecommunications rooms in the Maintenance and Warehouse Buildings; 
F. Installing fencing; 
G. Executing all work with minimal disruption to the City’s operational OT and IT networks.
Period of Performance: Work is to commence 30 days after Notice to Proceed, with substantial completion required within 210 days from Notice to Proceed.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed in Plant City, Florida, specifically at the site of the existing Public Works Building and adjacent facilities.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must have a minimum of three years documented experience in electrical service work and demonstrate satisfactory working relationships with local utility companies. 

Additionally, bidders must have Fiber Optic Specialty Contractor qualifications with at least five years of experience in installing fiber-optic systems similar in scope to this project.

Background: The Central Florida Tourism Oversight District (CFTOD) is a Special Taxing District that serves as a local government entity responsible for public infrastructure, including roads, bridges, and water control systems.

The goal of this contract is to enhance the facilities at the Solid Waste Transfer Station through various construction activities.
Work Details: The scope of work for the Solid Waste Transfer Station Admin Floors & Showers Project includes: 
