The contractor must furnish all labor, equipment, and materials necessary for the successful completion of the project while ensuring that essential household services remain operational during the work.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed as a one-time award via purchase order. The due date for submission of quotes is October 2, 2025, at which point work is expected to commence following contract award.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the property located at: 908 SW 3rd St, Delray Beach, FL 33444-0876.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be registered with the State of Florida Division of Corporations and have been in business for a minimum of five years prior to the due date. They must possess a Florida State General Contractor’s license or current certificate of competency issued by Palm Beach County Examining Board. Bidders are required to submit client references for similar services provided in the past three years. Additionally, bidders must not be listed on the Florida Department of Management Services Convicted Vendor List or on the SAM electronic roster of debarred companies.

Background: The Florida Department of Environmental Protection is issuing this addendum for the Guana Tolomato Matanzas National Estuarine Research Reserve North Boardwalk Reconstruction project, identified as DEP BID NO. BDC02-25/26. 
The purpose of this contract is to reconstruct the boardwalk at the reserve, which is part of the agency's mission to protect and manage Florida's natural resources.
Work Details: The project involves the reconstruction of the North Boardwalk at the Guana Tolomato Matanzas National Estuarine Research Reserve. 
Key requirements include: 
1) No permits are required from USACE, FDEP, or SJRWMD as the project is exempt; 
2) Additional county building permits are required; 
3) Equipment regulations specify that a rubber track mini excavator and an NPK vibrating compactor plate can be used, provided that top-down construction methods are employed to minimize impacts to dunes and vegetation; 
4) Mats may be required to minimize impact; 
5) Lumberock 2x6 Coastal Collection Decking can be used as an acceptable alternative to specified 2x6 composite decking if it meets or exceeds design standards.
Period of Performance: The contract performance period is not explicitly stated in the provided information.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the Guana Tolomato Matanzas National Estuarine Research Reserve located in Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must acknowledge receipt of this addendum by signing it and including it with their bid submission. 
Failure to do so may result in rejection of the bid.

Background: The City of Pompano Beach is seeking professional companies/firms to provide engineering services for the Water Treatment Plant under the Consultant’s Competitive Negotiation Act (CCNA), as outlined in Section 287.055, Florida Statutes. The goal of this contract is to engage qualified firms with specific experience and capabilities for various water treatment projects on a continuing as-needed basis.
Work Details: The selected firm will be responsible for a range of services including: 
- Preparing studies and recommending methods of operation; 
- Preparing preliminary design reports and design alternative recommendations; 
- Creating bidding/construction documents; 
- Attending pre-bid conferences and assisting in bid award recommendations; 
- Preparing permit applications; 
- Providing construction engineering/management services; 
- Project close-out services. 

Firms must have experience in municipal water and reuse treatment plant projects and be licensed to practice Professional Engineering in Florida.
Period of Performance: The contract will be for five (5) years with no renewals, commencing upon award by the appropriate City officials.
Place of Performance: Services will be performed at the Pompano Beach Water Treatment Plant, located in Pompano Beach, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Firms must be registered on the City’s eBid System to view solicitation documents. They are required to submit a Letter of Interest along with qualifications, references, and proof of financial solvency. Additionally, firms must comply with insurance requirements including general liability, professional liability, and workers' compensation insurance.

Background: The City of Coral Gables is seeking to retain the services of a qualified General Contractor and/or Miami-Dade County Certified Engineering Contractor for the purpose of repairing and rehabilitating the sewer collection system. This includes the replacement of sanitary sewer main and lateral pipelines, cured-in-place lining for sanitary sewer pipes, and rehabilitation of sanitary sewer manholes at various locations within the City on an as-needed basis.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
1) Sanitary Sewer Point Repairs (Mainlines and Laterals);
2) Sanitary Sewer Main and Laterals Replacement;
3) Sanitary Sewer Cleaning and TV Inspection (Mainlines and Laterals);
4) Cured-in-place Installation (e.g., Sectionals, Laterals liners);
5) Sanitary Manholes Rehabilitation;
6) Sanitary Sewer Manholes Replacement.

The awarded contractor must provide two dedicated crews, including one foreman and two laborers experienced in sewer system work. The contractor must also own or have guaranteed access to specific equipment such as a CCTV inspection system, trench excavation equipment capable of reaching depths up to 22 feet, and bypass pumping systems.
Period of Performance: The initial contract period is three years with an option to renew for two additional one-year periods at the sole discretion of the City. The contract may be extended for up to 180 days beyond the contract period if necessary.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at various locations within the City of Coral Gables, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must have been engaged in providing similar services for a minimum of five years, provide three references from similar engagements, hold an active license as a General Contractor or Miami-Dade County Certified Engineering Contractor, and demonstrate ownership or guaranteed access to required equipment. Key personnel must have five years of experience in sanitary sewer construction and rehabilitation, be trained in OSHA Confined Space Entry procedures, Florida Trench Safety Act compliance, and FDOT Maintenance of Traffic.

Background: The City of Hollywood, through its Community Redevelopment Agency (CRA), is seeking to procure services for the repair of trip hazards and drain gaps, along with color restoration and finishing of brick paver surfaces. This contract is intended to enhance public safety and aesthetic appeal in community areas.
Work Details: The services to be provided include:

1) Paver Repair of trip hazards and drain gaps;

2) Application of 'COLORBOOST', a special solvent-based formula infused with color enhancers that creates a new finish for brick pavers;

3) Micro-cleaning of paver surfaces prior to application, which involves multiple chemical applications, palm sanding, surface grinding, and high-pressure power washing;

4) Elimination of trip hazards by addressing deteriorated concrete sections;

5) Pressure cleaning and etching of water features to remove dirt, algae, and scaling;

6) Re-texturing damaged areas to match original designs using compatible stamped overlay techniques;

7) Application of a multi-layer elastomeric waterproof membrane for protection against water intrusion;

8) Sealing drain gaps with marine-grade flexible polyurethane joint sealant;

9) Color restoration and finishing to match original design schemes.
Period of Performance: The total duration for the completion of the work is approximately 7 to 10 days.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at various locations within the City of Hollywood, specifically targeting areas such as sidewalks, pool decks, patios, driveways, and public water features like Charnow Park.
Bidder Requirements: ColorBack Products Corp is identified as the sole source provider for the COLORBOOST system due to its unique formulation and exclusive rights. The vendor must hold appropriate liability insurance coverage as stipulated by the City.

Background: The City of Pembroke Pines is seeking bids from qualified firms to install pet-friendly artificial turf at the Main Police Station. This initiative aligns with the city's commitment to enhancing public spaces while ensuring they are safe and accommodating for pets. The goal of this contract is to provide a durable and environmentally friendly solution for the police station's outdoor areas.
Work Details: The contractor will be responsible for the installation of pet-friendly artificial turf at the Main Police Station. The scope of work includes:

1) Preparation of the site, including removal of existing grass and debris;

2) Installation of a base layer suitable for artificial turf;

3) Installation of high-quality, pet-friendly artificial turf that meets specified standards;

4) Ensuring proper drainage and maintenance access;

5) Providing warranties and product specifications as required.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed over a period of three months from the date of award.
Place of Performance: The installation will take place at the Main Police Station located in Pembroke Pines, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must have experience in similar installations and provide proof of relevant licenses and insurance. Vendors must also comply with all applicable federal, state, and local laws pertaining to public works projects.

Background: The City of Coral Gables is seeking to engage a qualified Construction Manager at Risk (CMR) firm for the successful completion of the City Hall Renovation and Restoration Project. The CMR will provide preconstruction services expertise during the design phase and subsequently serve as the general contractor during construction, assuming risk through a guaranteed maximum price or fixed price contract.
Work Details: The Contractor will provide all materials, supervision, labor, tools, and equipment necessary to complete the work in accordance with the Contract Documents. This includes:

1) Construction of the City Hall Renovation and Restoration Project;
2) Providing preconstruction services;
3) Serving as general contractor during construction;
4) Ensuring compliance with applicable laws, including Florida Building Code;
5) Furnishing required surety bonds and insurance;
6) Managing all aspects of project execution including labor, administration, management, supervision, testing, services, materials, supplies, equipment, fixtures, appliances, facilities, tools, transportation, storage, power, permits and licenses.
Period of Performance: The work shall commence upon execution of the Agreement or issuance of a Notice to Proceed and must be substantially completed within one thousand ninety-five (1,095) calendar days. Final completion is required no later than thirty (30) calendar days after delivery of the Punch List.
Place of Performance: The project will be performed at 405 Biltmore Way, Coral Gables, FL 33134.
Bidder Requirements: The Contractor must provide a Payment and Performance Bond as per Section 255.05 of Florida Statutes. Additionally, the Contractor must comply with all applicable laws regarding insurance and bonding requirements.

Background: The City of Fort Lauderdale, Florida, is seeking bids for construction services at Holiday Park, located at 1150 G. Harold Martin Drive, Fort Lauderdale, FL 33304. This project is part of the Parks and Recreation Department's initiative to enhance public parks and recreational facilities. The goal is to improve the park's infrastructure and amenities to better serve the community.
Work Details: The project includes extensive construction services such as: 
- Demolition of existing structures including playgrounds, lighting, and fencing; 
- Grading and drainage improvements; 
- Installation of a new irrigation system; 
- Landscaping with new trees, palms, shrubs, and sod; 
- Construction of a new playground area with equipment and safety surfacing; 
- Enhancements to dog park facilities including concrete pads and seating; 
- Installation of new sidewalks and signage throughout the park; 
- Various site enhancements like benches, tables, trash receptacles, and shade structures for sports fields. 

Specific tasks include root removal, stump grinding, erosion control measures, and adjustments to existing storm drainage structures.
Period of Performance: The contract work is expected to be completed within the number of calendar days stipulated in the contract following the issuance of a Notice to Proceed (NTP).
Place of Performance: All work will be performed at Holiday Park located at 1150 G. Harold Martin Drive, Fort Lauderdale, FL 33304.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess appropriate licenses as described in the Contract Documents. Additionally, all subcontractors must comply with the City’s Code of Ordinances at the time of the pre-construction conference.

Background: Miami-Dade County's People and Internal Operations Department (PIOD) is soliciting proposals for construction and renovation services under Project No. W230030-C. The project aims to renovate the interior of the West Dade Government Center, a 6-story office building, enhancing the functionality and aesthetics of floors 1 through 4.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
- Selective demolition of partitions, finishes, and ceilings;
- Renovation of existing offices;
- Installation of new floor and wall finishes;
- New ceiling tiles in existing grids;
- Redistribution of existing furniture;
- Replacement of lights, AC grills, and sprinkler heads in existing grids;
- Reconfiguration of select offices with new interior partitions, finishes, furniture, doors, ceilings, and light fixtures;
- Adjustments to existing mechanical/electrical/low-voltage systems;
- Construction of new restrooms and breakroom;
- Installation of a new impact-resistant storefront entrance;
- Creation of a reception/information/check-in desk with turnstiles/secured access;
- Installation of new ADA ramps and lifts;
- Addition of monitors and kiosks.

The contractor may perform work 24/7 based on availability.
Place of Performance: 9250 W. Flagler Street, Miami, Florida 33174.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must have experience as a Prime Contractor with a minimum of eight (8) years in similar projects or five (5) completed projects. They must possess applicable construction licensing or Miami-Dade County Contractor’s Certification in relevant categories. A certified check or acceptable bid bond for at least 5% of the base bid is required. Bidders must also provide safety record documentation upon request.

Background: The Housing and Community Services Department of the City of Hialeah, Florida, is seeking experienced and qualified contractors for construction services at the Gladys Zogpy property located at 3730 East 2nd Avenue, Hialeah, FL 33013. The goal of this contract is to enhance the living conditions of the property through various renovations and improvements.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
1. Roof replacement;
2. Replacement of windows and doors;
3. Replacement of HVAC equipment;
4. Duct cleaning;
5. Remodeling of a second bathroom;
6. Replacement of laminated flooring in the living room;
7. Removal and repair of popcorn ceilings in the living area, bathroom, two bedrooms, and kitchen;
8. Repair of steps in the primary bedroom;
9. Repair and installation of doors for a patio metal shed.
Period of Performance: The contract work is expected to commence within fifteen (15) calendar days from the issuance of a Notice to Proceed and must be completed within ninety (90) calendar days from that date.
Place of Performance: All work will be performed at the Gladys Zogpy property located at 3730 East 2nd Avenue, Hialeah, FL 33013.
Bidder Requirements: Contractors must be fully licensed in the State of Florida and demonstrate expertise, financial stability, and a proven track record in similar projects. Additionally, they are required to provide proof of current state and county certification in Florida.

Background: The City of Fort Lauderdale, Florida, is seeking bids for construction services at the Annie Beck House located in Middle River Park Terrace Park. This project is managed by the City's Public Works Department and aims to enhance the historic structure following the City’s Historic Preservation Design Guidelines.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
- Upgrades to hardscape and landscape elements;
- Repairs to the porch and deck;
- Installation of new louvers;
- Façade and window restoration;
- Cleaning of composition roof tiles;
- Complete interior repainting;
- Sanding and refinishing of interior flooring.

The project consists of five drawing sheets available for free on the City’s online strategic sourcing platform.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed from the date of award until completion, with specific timelines to be determined based on project requirements.
Place of Performance: Middle River Park Terrace Park, 1329 NE 7th Avenue, Fort Lauderdale, Florida 33304.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess a current Professional Registration license or General Contractor’s license issued by the State of Florida. All subcontractors must also be licensed and insured. A bid security in the form of a certified check or bid bond for ten percent (10%) of the bid amount is required. Bidders must submit proof of insurance and required licenses/certifications with their bids.

Background: The City of Plantation is seeking bids for the Deicke Auditorium Roof Replacement and Structural Repairs project. The goal of this contract is to replace the existing roof system, ensuring compliance with current building and wind codes. This project aims to enhance the safety and functionality of the auditorium, which serves as a community venue.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
1) Removal and replacement of the existing standing seam metal roofing system;
2) Installation of new plywood sheathing;
3) Retrofit work on the roof structure to comply with current building codes;
4) Installation of insulation, including tapered insulation on the roof;
5) Replacement of damaged wood decking (2" and 3" wood planks);
6) Installation of new gutters and downspouts;
7) Mechanical work including ductwork and condensate lines;
8) Electrical work including conduit and wiring;
9) Plumbing work including new roof drains;
10) General cleanup and miscellaneous repairs to adjacent surfaces affected by construction.
Period of Performance: The contract work is expected to be completed within 210 calendar days from the notice to proceed.
Place of Performance: The performance will take place at Deicke Auditorium, located in Plantation, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must be licensed general contractors with a minimum of five years’ experience in roofing projects. They must have successfully completed at least three similar projects in Florida within the last five years. Bidders are required to submit a bid bond, insurance documentation, and comply with all local regulations regarding construction.

Background: The City of Fort Lauderdale, Florida is seeking bids from qualified contractors to provide construction services for the Fort Lauderdale Executive Airport. The goal of this contract is to ensure the proper maintenance and sealing of Runway 13-31, which is critical for the airport's operations. This project is part of the city's commitment to maintaining safe and efficient airport facilities.
Work Details: The work under this contract includes:
1. Clearing existing pavement;
2. Joint and crack repair;
3. Pavement marking;
4. Seal coating of Runway 13-31.

All work must comply with current codes and regulations, as well as adhere to the provided drawings and specifications.
Period of Performance: The contract will be performed over a specified period as outlined in the proposal, with completion expected within a defined timeframe following the issuance of a Notice to Proceed.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Fort Lauderdale Executive Airport (FXE), located in Fort Lauderdale, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must demonstrate competency and financial responsibility by providing evidence of past experience on similar projects, a list of equipment, and key personnel available for the work. Additionally, bidders must comply with prequalification regulations set by the Owner and may need to submit a bid bond or certified check as collateral.

Background: The City of Hollywood, Florida, is a beachfront community located in southeastern Broward County. The City operates a Water Treatment Plant that utilizes a softening treatment process involving catalyst/sand blend and lime. This process produces spent catalyst sand and lime sludge as by-products that require disposal. The City is seeking qualified contractors for the disposal of these materials in accordance with specified terms and conditions.
Work Details: The contractor will be responsible for the loading, transporting, and disposal of municipal water treatment plant lime sludge and catalyst sand. Specific responsibilities include:

1) Loading and hauling materials from the designated location to approved disposal sites while ensuring the holding area remains operational;

2) Performing services at designated times without disrupting ongoing operations;

3) Ensuring all equipment is in good working order and free of leaks;

4) Selecting authorized dumping sites and providing proof of proper dumping;

5) Implementing dust control methods if required;

6) Maintaining roads free of spilled materials;

7) Repairing any damage to public or private property;

8) Providing an approved container for hauling lime sludge;

9) Timely removal of catalyst to keep access clear for facility vehicles.
Period of Performance: The contract will commence upon award and is expected to last for two years, with potential renewals for two additional two-year terms. Services will be scheduled on an 'as needed' basis, with pick-ups typically scheduled on a full truckload basis within forty-eight hours of notification.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the City of Hollywood Water Treatment Plant located at 3441 Hollywood Blvd., Hollywood, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must have at least two years of experience in providing similar disposal services. They must demonstrate sufficient financial support and capability to perform the required services. Additionally, bidders must comply with insurance requirements including general liability, vehicle liability, workers' compensation, and pollution liability insurance.

Background: The Florida Department of Health is seeking competitive prices for interior painting services for six specified buildings at the Miami-Dade County Health Department (CHD). 
The goal of this contract is to ensure the facilities are properly maintained and visually appealing, which aligns with the Department's mission to promote public health.
Work Details: The contractor will provide painting services that include preparation, cleaning, caulking, and painting the interiors of the following buildings: 
1) Health District Center, 1350 NW 14 St, Miami, FL 33125; 
2) Little Haiti Clinic, 300 NE 80th Terrace, Miami, FL 33138; 
3) West Flagler, 2515 West Flagler Street, Miami, FL 33135; 
4) West Perrine Clinic, 18255 Homestead Ave, Miami FL 33157; 
5) Liberty City Clinic, 2520 NW 75 St, Miami FL 33147; 
6) Golden Glades, 1725 NW 167th Street, Miami, FL 33056. 
The work includes obtaining necessary permits within 20 days of order issuance and completing tasks in three phases: 
Phase 1 involves preparing walls by removing contaminants; 
Phase 2 includes caulking and patching damaged surfaces; 
Phase 3 consists of applying two coats of Sherwin Williams SuperPaint interior Acrylic Latex on walls and wood surfaces and two coats of Sherwin Williams Pro Industrial Multi Surface Acrylic on metal surfaces. 
All work must comply with manufacturer instructions.
Period of Performance: The contract will commence on September 1, 2025 or upon issuance of the purchase order and will conclude at midnight on June 30, 2026.
Place of Performance: The services will be performed at six locations within Miami-Dade County as specified above.
Bidder Requirements: Respondents must have experience in painting large or commercial buildings with a minimum of five similar projects completed. 
They must also comply with background screening requirements for staff working under this contract. Additionally, bidders are encouraged to be certified minority or women-owned businesses.

Background: The City of North Miami Beach, FL is soliciting sealed responses for the prequalification of general contractors for upcoming construction projects. This process aims to ensure that contractors meet the necessary financial, technical, and performance standards required to successfully complete projects in accordance with the City's quality, safety, and regulatory requirements. Contractors will be assessed based on their experience, financial stability, past performance, safety record, and compliance with applicable laws and regulations. Those who qualify will be placed on a prequalified bidders list for future solicitations.
Work Details: Contractors must demonstrate:
1) Business information including length of time in business and references;
2) Adequate bonding capacity for 100% Payment and Performance Construction Bonds;
3) Experience as a prime contractor for at least five governmental or commercial buildings costing at least $5 million each;
4) Completion of at least three buildings of a minimum of 12,000 square feet;
5) Completion of at least three green buildings with one being LEED Certified;
6) Completion of one governmental site development project;
7) A satisfactory safety record judged by OSHA citations;
8) Valid Florida General Contractor’s License;
9) Financial capacity to complete projects valued at a minimum of $5 million;
10) No bankruptcy declarations in the last five years.

Additionally, contractors must maintain insurance including Worker’s Compensation, General Liability, Automobile Liability, and Builder’s Risk with Windstorm Coverage.
Period of Performance: The prequalification process will assess contractors annually or as needed at the City's discretion.
Place of Performance: The geographic location for the work will be within the City of North Miami Beach.
Bidder Requirements: Contractors must have valid licenses and insurance coverage as specified. They should also demonstrate financial stability and past performance without any significant litigation or claims against them in the last five years. Participation from diverse contractors including small, minority, and women-owned businesses is encouraged.

Background: Toho Water Authority, established in October 2003, is the largest provider of water, wastewater, and reclaimed water services in Osceola County. The agency's mission is to provide reliable, cost-effective, and responsive water services while protecting public health and the environment.

This Request for Proposal (RFP) seeks qualified firms to establish General Services Agreements for Instrumentation and Control Services related to emergent, emergency, or time-critical work in water and wastewater systems.
Work Details: The Contractor(s) shall provide professional services for Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition (SCADA) planning, designing, and integration including subsystems such as electrical, instrumentation, servers, and network communications as they relate to the utility SCADA system.

Specific tasks include:
- Furnishing and installing new instrumentation and Programmable Logic Controllers (PLCs);
- Programming PLCs;
- Programming Human Machine Interfaces (HMI) and Operator Interface Terminal (OIT);
- In-plant SCADA networking;
- Demolition and disposal of existing facilities and equipment;
- Staff supplement;
- Supplying control panels as specified by Toho;
- Troubleshooting and repairing control systems;
- Instrumentation installation, modification, and repair;
- Furnishing, fabricating, and installing electrical and instrumentation panels;
- Documentation of existing and as-built electrical wiring; 
- Other related services.
Period of Performance: The initial contract period shall be for three (3) years commencing upon execution of a contract for this award. The contract may be renewed for one (1) additional two (2) year period subject to written agreement by both parties.
Place of Performance: Services will be performed within the Toho Water Authority service area located in Osceola County.
Bidder Requirements: Proposers must have a minimum of five (5) years of experience managing instrumentation and controls for utility systems. They must reside within 100 miles from Toho Water Authority service area. Proposers must be an Allen-Bradley Certified Systems Integrator – Silver Level or higher & Water/Wastewater Certified.

Additionally, preferences include having staff with Global Industrial Cyber Security Professional Certificate (GICSP), Cisco Certified Network Associate Certification (CCNA), or Fortinet Network Security Expert (NSE) Certification.

Background: The Miami-Dade County Public Library System (MDPLS) is seeking construction services for the Replacement Key Biscayne Branch Library. The goal of this project is to replace the existing 6,200 square foot library built in 1976 with a new two-story library that will be approximately 20,000 square feet. The new facility aims to meet modern technological standards and sustainable building practices, including LEED silver certification.
Work Details: The contractor shall review all documents, plans, and scope of work provided by MDPLS. The work includes:

- Demolition of the existing library;
- Site construction while protecting existing landscaping and water features;
- Construction of a new two-story library with sustainable features such as rooftop solar panels and electric vehicle charging stations;
- Interior finishes including ceilings, paint, flooring, accessories, and fixtures;
- Installation of state-of-the-art audio/visual systems;
- Providing a new water line on adjacent Key Colony property within the first 90 days after Notice to Proceed (NTP).

The contractor must hire an experienced low voltage/media professional (Integrator) to coordinate all systems and ensure compliance with standards. All work must comply with applicable building codes and obtain necessary approvals from relevant authorities.
Period of Performance: The project is estimated to take 669 calendar days from the start date, with specific milestones such as completing the water line relocation within the first 90 days after NTP.
Place of Performance: The contract will be performed at 299 Crandon Boulevard, Key Biscayne, Florida 33149.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must hold a valid Certified General Contractor license and provide documentation demonstrating experience in multi-story commercial or public building construction using sustainable materials within the last five years. Experience with library technologies and LEED certified projects is preferred. Bidders must also be fully insured and bonded for the project estimated at $20,594,556.13.

Description:
The City of Winter Haven is seeking professional services related to the design and future construction of a water administration facility.
The scope of professional services that are required by this contract award resulting under this RFQ is anticipated to include, but not be limited to, design criteria package professional services and services that are typically associated with an Owner&rsquo;s Representative and oversight (CEI-type services) of a municipal capital project.&nbsp; The expectation is that the entity, individual, or firm awarded the contract would work in concert with designated City representatives for the preparation of the Design Criteria Package and represent the City for the selected Design Build (DB) team for the Utility Administration Facility, Resource Center, and Operations Center to provide oversight and management throughout the entire project including project design and permitting review; pre-construction services; construction oversight and related services; funding compliance and project close out as described below.
&nbsp;

Documents AI Summary:
Background: The Florida Department of Corrections (FDC) is the largest agency in Florida and operates the third-largest state prison system in the United States. The FDC manages 143 facilities statewide, including major institutions, work camps, and community release centers.

This Invitation to Bid (ITB) aims to secure responsive bids from responsible vendors for plumbing installation, materials, parts, and repair services for various correctional institutions throughout the state. The goal is to establish a new Agency Term Contract (ATC) to ensure efficient plumbing services across these facilities.
Work Details: The successful vendor will provide comprehensive plumbing installation, materials, parts, and repair services as specified in Attachment I – Price Sheet. Services include:
1) Installation, repair or replacement of drain, waste, supply lines;
2) Installation and servicing of plumbing fixtures such as faucets, commodes, sinks;
3) Repair and replacement of potable water lines;
4) Cleaning of sanitary sewer lines;
5) Leak detection at various heights;
6) Backflow testing and repairs;
7) Emergency service calls requiring immediate response;
8) Non-emergency service calls with a qualified technician on-site within specified timeframes.

The vendor must supply all labor, tools, materials, and equipment necessary for these services.
Period of Performance: The contract will be awarded for a term of up to five years with potential renewals as specified under Section 287.057(14), Florida Statutes.
Place of Performance: Services will be performed at various correctional institutions throughout the State of Florida as listed in Attachment V – Service/Delivery Locations.
Bidder Requirements: Vendors must have certified technicians with at least five years of relevant experience. They must comply with state licensing requirements and be registered in the MyFloridaMarketPlace Vendor Information Portal (VIP).

Additionally, vendors are required to submit mandatory documentation including a Price Sheet, Drug-Free Workplace Certification, Security Requirements for Contractors, and other specified attachments. Vendors must also disclose any anticipated subcontracts at the time of bid submission.

Background: The Central Florida Tourism Oversight District (CFTOD) is seeking proposals from experienced and qualified firms for the permanent abandonment and removal of sections of the High Temperature Hot Water (HTHW) hotel loop serving the Magic Kingdom Resort Area. 
This project includes all associated demolition, restoration, permitting, and coordination in accordance with Reedy Creek Energy Services (RCES), CFTOD, and Walt Disney World (WDW) requirements.
Work Details: The contractor will be responsible for the following tasks: 
- Permanent abandonment and removal of the remaining sections of the HTHW hotel loop; 
- Associated demolition; 
- Restoration of affected areas; 
- Obtaining necessary permits; 
- Coordinating with RCES/CFTOD/WDW to ensure compliance with all requirements. 
The contractor must hold specific certifications including ASME/ANSI B31.1 Certification, Advanced TTC Certification, and Basic Flagger TTC Certification.
Period of Performance: The contract's performance period is not explicitly stated in the provided solicitation details.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at the Magic Kingdom Resort Area in Lake Buena Vista, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must possess ASME/ANSI B31.1 Certification, Advanced TTC Certification, and Basic Flagger TTC Certification. 
Additionally, bidders are required to register on the PlanetBids platform to participate in the bidding process.

Background: The Elevated Water Tank Demolition Project, City Project No. 21-0020-UT, is initiated by the City of Clearwater. The project aims to demolish and remove two one-million-gallon steel elevated water storage tanks along with all associated appurtenances. The goal is to restore the sites completely after the demolition activities are completed.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
1) Demolition, removal, and disposal of two (2) one-million-gallon steel elevated water storage tanks and all appurtenances;
2) Complete dismantling and removal of all tank components at both sites;
3) Site restoration upon completion of demolition activities;
4) Specific tasks include:
a) Removal of the North Elevated Water Tank located on Weston Drive and the South Elevated Water Tank located on South Martin Luther King Jr. Avenue;
b) Cutting foundation piles to a final elevation of 6 feet above grade level;
c) Removal of site features within a 6-foot depth around each tank including concrete slabs, fencing, piping, conduits, valves, etc.;
d) Providing a layout by a licensed surveyor for remaining elements post-demolition;
e) Cutting and capping existing water lines outside fenced areas;
f) Delivery or pick-up of salvaged materials from the demolition project;
g) Site cleanup including grading and resodding after debris removal.
Period of Performance: The estimated duration for completing the project is 210 calendar days.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at two locations in Clearwater, Florida: Weston Drive for the North Elevated Water Tank and South Martin Luther King Jr. Avenue for the South Elevated Water Tank.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must demonstrate qualifications by providing references for previous projects involving demolition of elevated steel drinking water tanks with similar capacity. They must also hold current licenses/registrations with the State of Florida and Pinellas County. Contractors are responsible for securing all necessary permits.

Background: The Cruise Terminal 5 Marine Improvements project is initiated by the Canaveral Port Authority, aiming to enhance the operational capabilities of Cruise Terminal 5 at Port Canaveral. The project involves significant structural upgrades to existing marine facilities, ensuring compliance with safety and operational standards.
Work Details: The scope of work includes:
- Selective demolition of the existing open-pile concrete pier and adjacent mooring dolphins;
- Construction of new open pile concrete pier extensions to the north and south;
- Installation of mooring fixtures and marine fenders;
- Construction of new steel monopile mooring dolphins;
- Modification and reinstallation of existing aluminum catwalks;
- Modification of the electrical raceway system and potable water lines;
- Repairs to existing pier deck joints and curbs;
- Installation of new concrete curbs and handrails;
- Procurement and installation of steel pipe piles, precast/prestressed concrete piles, precast/prestressed deck units, stainless steel ladders, marine fenders, and mooring fixtures;
- Design, procurement, and installation of a solar-powered lighting system;
- Dive inspections and surveys to verify existing conditions.
Period of Performance: The contract will be executed from July 2025 through July 2026, with critical milestones aligned with cruise vessel schedules.
Place of Performance: The work will be performed at Cruise Terminal 5, located in Port Canaveral, Florida.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must comply with all local regulations regarding permits (USACE and FDEP) and adhere to safety standards. They are required to provide a list of intended suppliers for Owner-Purchased Materials as part of their bid submission.

Background: The City of Coral Gables, Florida, is seeking bids for roof and tower repairs at the Coral Gables Country Club, an iconic landmark built in 1922. 
The purpose of this solicitation is to engage a qualified and experienced General Contractor to perform necessary repairs to ensure the structural integrity and aesthetic appeal of this historic site.
Work Details: The work generally consists of: 
- General Conditions; 
- Mobilization; 
- Structural work including shoring design and installation; 
- Structural work items as detailed in drawing S1.04; 
- Wind pressure calculations; 
- A/C unit screen framing; 
- Tower repairs. 
The project will be deemed complete upon successful completion of these tasks as determined by the City, ensuring each item meets project specifications.
Period of Performance: The work is expected to be substantially completed within ninety (90) calendar days from the commencement date stated in the Notice to Proceed. 
Final completion will occur thirty (30) calendar days thereafter.
Place of Performance: The contract will be performed at the Coral Gables Country Club located at 997 N. Greenway Drive, Coral Gables, FL 33134.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must demonstrate a minimum of three (3) years of experience as a General Contractor providing similar construction services. 
They must provide at least three references for similar projects completed in the last three years, hold an active license with the Florida Department of Business and Professional Regulation as a General Contractor, and comply with all local occupational license requirements.

Background: The City of Coral Gables, Florida, is seeking bids for the replacement of doors and windows at the Coral Gables Country Club, an iconic landmark built in 1922. The purpose of this solicitation is to engage a qualified and experienced General Contractor to carry out this project, enhancing the facility's functionality and aesthetics.
Work Details: The scope of work includes: 
- General Conditions; 
- Mobilization; 
- Architectural work for a Café Door; 
- Architectural work for an Arcade Door; 
- Architectural work for Windows. 

The project will be deemed complete upon successful completion of these tasks as determined by the City, ensuring each item meets project specifications. Detailed plans are provided in Exhibit A and Exhibit B prepared by Ferguson, Glasgow, Schuster, Soto and Wood/O’Donnell & Naccarato respectively.
Period of Performance: The work is expected to be substantially completed within 120 calendar days from the commencement date stated in the Notice to Proceed. Final completion will occur 30 calendar days after substantial completion.
Place of Performance: The contract will be performed at the Coral Gables Country Club located at 997 N. Greenway Drive, Coral Gables, FL 33134.
Bidder Requirements: Bidders must have a minimum of three years of experience as a General Contractor providing similar construction services. They must provide at least three references for similar projects completed in the last three years. Additionally, bidders must hold an active license with the Department of Business and Professional Regulation of Florida.
